        DASH1["SYSTEM HEALTH DASHBOARD + LIVE CONTROL CENTER<br>BUILD NEW | TWO LAYERS:<br>LAYER 1 - WEEKLY DASHBOARD (Monday morning review - trend analysis):<br>UNIT: Prospect-level (deduplicated by lp_prospect_id)<br>ATTRIBUTION: First-touch source for all source-level metrics<br>METRICS: Traffic by source (7) | Lead capture rate | Bridge completion<br>Buyer stage distribution | Indoc completion | VSL watch %<br>Booking rate by appt type | Show rate | Close rate<br>Seinfeld re-engagement | Objection distribution<br>Referral rate | LTV by entry source<br>LP SYNC HEALTH: sync lag | failure rate | trigger success rate<br>Day 15 handoff volume | LP disposition distribution of reactivation candidates<br>ALERT THRESHOLDS:<br>Lead capture below 10% | Bridge completion below 50%<br>VSL watch below 25% at 50% mark | Booking below 15%<br>Show rate below 60% | Close rate below 20%<br>Seinfeld re-engagement below 5%<br>Unmapped LP sources above 10 new/week<br>LAYER 2 - LIVE CONTROL CENTER (v6.12 - real-time visibility):<br>IMPLEMENTATION: Supabase materialized views refreshed on schedule + GHL webhooks<br>DISPLAY: Notion dashboard (MVP) then custom React dashboard (Phase 2)<br>ALERTS: GroupMe notifications when thresholds breached<br>6 LIVE PANELS:<br>P1: Stall Detection - prospects per stage, avg dwell time, 2x dwell = bottleneck alert (hourly)<br>P2: Momentum Capture Rate - signals detected vs converted to booking, miss rate (15 min)<br>P3: Drop-Off Clusters - neg-signal heat map by workflow step, underperforming content (daily)<br>P4: Source Tier Performance - FT prospect close rate by tier, revenue per prospect (daily)<br>P5: Sprint Performance - which reactivation angle converting, response rate by sprint (per sprint)<br>P6: Referral Engine - asks sent by trigger point, conversion by trigger, pipeline value (daily)<br>SUPABASE VIEWS TO BUILD:<br>  mv_stall_detection: stage, count, avg_days_in_stage, bottleneck_flag<br>  mv_momentum_capture: signal_type, detected_count, captured_count, miss_count, capture_rate<br>  mv_negative_signals: workflow_id, step_id, neg_signal_type, count, pct_of_total<br>  mv_source_tier_live: ft_source, tier, prospects, close_rate, revenue, demo_rate<br>  mv_sprint_performance: sprint_number, angle, sent, replied, booked, conversion_rate<br>  mv_referral_engine: trigger_point, asks_sent, referrals_received, referral_close_rate<br>GHL WEBHOOK EVENTS TO CAPTURE:<br>  appointment.created | appointment.cancelled | contact_tag.added | contact_tag.removed<br>  funnel_pageview | email.opened | email.clicked | sms.replied<br>  These events flow to Supabase via Railway webhook receiver<br>  Materialized views refresh on schedule: P1 hourly, P2 every 15 min, P3-P6 daily<br>FEEDBACK LOOP: Panel 3 (drop-off clusters) feeds directly into content decisions<br>  If SA1 Hurricane has 40% drop-off at Step 3 of S2.0 = rewrite that email<br>  If sprint 2 (social proof) converts 3x better than sprint 1 (code compliance) = lead with social proof<br>  The system does not just measure. It INFORMS the next content iteration."]
